1.0E+05     PressureDrop: difference in fluid pressure (in Pa) between inside and outside; applied (maximum) pressure from IN.sigma...
150         Np: number of pressure points in output
0.12        width (in cm) of rectangular seal in fluid flow direction, or diameter (in cm) of O-ring: only used if iflag008=4, 5, 40 or 50 
0           irepeat: if = 1 and iflag008=4 or 5 or 40 or 50 --> deformation of seal done fast; assumes iflag008=1 or 2 done to prepare input data

0.8         spc: when contact area percolate replace sigmaeff(p) in percolated region (p>pc) with sigmaeff(spc*pc) for O-ring 
10000       Nx: integer number of x-values fot p(x),u(x): must be large to get converged resuly, Nx ~ 10^4 (or more) for O-ring (iflag008=4 or 5)        
3000000     Npa: integer number of fluid pressures: must be large to get converged resuly, Npa ~ 3x10^6 (or more) for O-ring (iflag008=4 or 5)         
0.99        old: mix old and new to get converged result for O-ring (iflag008=4 or 5)


0.1E+05     gas pressure (in Pa) on high pressure side (for gas leakage) (1 atm is added)
0.0         gas pressure (in Pa) on low pressure side (for gas leakage) (1 atm is added)
1.76E-05    gas viscosity (in Pas) (for gas leakage; for liquid leakage it is in IN.FLUID...); He: 1.96E-05 Pas, N2: 1.76E-05 Pas at T=20C
471.0       barv=average speed of gas molecule (for gas leakage) barv=sqrt(8*kB*T/pi*m); He: 1255 m/s; N2: 471 m/s at T=20C
20.0        temperature in Celsius (for gas leakage)
